voltaic (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Show a tray icon on Wayland. The automatic backend order tried XEmbed
    first, which under Wayland constructs without error and then displays
    nothing, so Voltaic ran with no icon and no complaint. Affected GNOME
    and KDE on Wayland, the default session on current Ubuntu and Fedora.
  * Report why there is no tray icon, in a notification and on stderr,
    rather than running invisibly.
  * The empty panel no longer tells AirPods-only users to check a Logitech
    receiver they do not own.
  * Fix a PyGIWarning from importing Gdk without a version guard.

 -- jcfs <jcfs@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0000

voltaic (1.2.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix source installs on Debian and Ubuntu, which need python3-venv for
    python3 -m venv to work at all.
  * Fix source installs on openSUSE, where the GTK typelib lives in
    typelib-1_0-Gtk-3_0 rather than gtk3.
  * install.sh now verifies that GTK is importable after installing it,
    rather than trusting the package manager's exit code, and works when
    run as root or on a machine with no udev.
  * Continuous integration now runs install.sh on Debian, Ubuntu, Fedora,
    Arch and openSUSE, and builds the Arch package.

 -- jcfs <jcfs@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:30:00 +0000

voltaic (1.2.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Published to a signed apt repository at https://jcfs.github.io/voltaic,
    so updates arrive with apt upgrade rather than by hand.
  * Manual page, Debian-format changelog and DEP-5 copyright: the package is
    now lintian-clean.
  * AppStream metadata, so the app appears in software centres with a
    description and screenshots.

 -- jcfs <jcfs@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 15 Aug 2026 09:00:00 +0000

voltaic (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Debian package, PKGBUILD and install.sh: installing is now one command
    on every major distribution.
  * The package ships the udev rules and replays them against an
    already-connected receiver, so no manual setup or replugging is needed.
  * Manual page and AppStream metadata.

 -- jcfs <jcfs@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 14 Aug 2026 17:00:00 +0000

voltaic (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Application icon, installed into the hicolor theme.
  * Report missing GTK dependencies in a dialog rather than dying with a
    traceback that a desktop launcher discards.
  * Distinguish a missing Bluetooth stack from having no accessories paired.
  * Headless unit tests and continuous integration.

